course: dictionary
lesson: 1732
title: Short words for measuring and symbols
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «cl» is a short way to write centilitre, a unit for measuring liquids such as juice or water. A litre is 100 centilitres, so 1 litre = 100 cl. A bottle that says 75 cl holds 75 centilitres of drink.
explain: Look at the capital letters. «Cl» with a capital C and small l is the chemical symbol for chlorine, not a measure. The sentence «Each element has a short symbol: Na for sodium, Cl for chlorine» uses Cl as the name of an element.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. On a juice bottle, cl means an amount of drink. In a science text about elements, Cl means chlorine. Ask yourself: is this about how much liquid, or about an element? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it makes sense.
fact: cl is short for centilitre, a unit for measuring liquid.
fact: 1 litre = 100 cl, and 1 cl = 10 ml.
fact: Bottles and cans often show cl on the label, such as 75 cl or 33 cl.
fact: «Cl» with a capital C is the chemical symbol for chlorine.
fact: Check the capital letter: cl means a measure, and Cl means an element.
exercise: The bottle says 75 cl. What does cl stand for? | Chlorine | Centimetre | Kilolitre | *Centilitre
exercise: How many millilitres are in 1 cl? | 1000 | 100 | 1 | *10
exercise: «Each element has a short symbol: Na for sodium, Cl for chlorine.» What does Cl mean here? | A litre of juice | *Chlorine, an element | A measure of liquid | A 33 cl can
test: How many centilitres are in 1 litre? | 10 | 1 | 1000 | *100
test: A 33 cl can holds how many millilitres? | *330 | 3300 | 33 | 3
exam: The label says 50 cl. How many millilitres is that? | 5 | 50 | *500 | 5000
